    "language": "en",
    "md5": "bc2751d11c187e806aff5d58606bd6e2",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1641,
    "chunk_text": "Choco-Tom Reunion: A Toyland Anecdote\n\nDear Meth, I was highly pleased when you found me in my home garden where the lawn had undergone so much damage as a result of the Cyclonic Storm Ditwah in the days. November 26-December 04, 2025. The sense of security I felt in your hands urged me to tell you who I am, what sort of a past I had, and how I feel now.\n\nHaving lost contact with my mother, I had been extremely sad and frustrated. I had almost lost hopes about seeing her again. But my dream of sitting in the lap of my mother became a reality once again when you reported to my former guardians, Gamini and Dammi, about your finding me in the wet lawn. I remember with pleasure how they quickly brought my mother back to me and placed me in her lap as I used to sit before. So I am again a happy bear kid enjoying the warmth of my mother.\n\nFor the last thirty five years, my home has been an old house called \u201cBellaria\u201d, situated in BANDARAWELA, in the salubrious cool climes of Sri Lanka. My former guardians, Gamini and Dammi, treated my mother \u201cChoco\u201d, in whose lap I have been always seated, and me, \u201cTom\u201d, with tremendous love and care. They gave us our names, based on our skin colours. My mother is dark chocolate brown in complexion, so they named her \u201cChoco\u201d, and I am tomato orange in complexion, and they named me \u201cTom\u201d.\n\nWe came to Sri Lanka from the small peninsula town called Gl\u00fccksburg-Holnis, in Northern Germany in October 1990. When Gamini visited Germany at that time, we were presented to him by our previous guardian, Dora. From Germany we made our trip via Switzerland, Scotland, and England."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-01-03-islandlk-28ab9352",
    "num": "islandlk-28ab9352",
    "date_str": "2026-01-03",
    "description": "Choco-Tom Reunion: A Toyland Anecdote",
    "url_metadata": "http://island.lk/choco-tom-reunion-a-toyland-anecdote/",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "islandlk",
    "time_ut": 1767435960.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-01-03-islandlk-28ab9352-0001",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "1a135409da9b97546bb61a948bbabe37",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1855,
    "chunk_text": "We came to Sri Lanka from the small peninsula town called Gl\u00fccksburg-Holnis, in Northern Germany in October 1990. When Gamini visited Germany at that time, we were presented to him by our previous guardian, Dora. From Germany we made our trip via Switzerland, Scotland, and England.\n\nAbout 36 years ago, when we came out of a toy factory in Germany together with hundreds of bear mothers and bear children, I was wondering whether we could make any significant impact on the humans we would meet. We were all packed in small boxes and transported to toy shops. I was relieved when we were taken out of our box and set on a shelf in a showcase in a toy shop. While sitting in my mother\u2019s lap, I kept gazing at the visitors to the shop. Small girls and boys found us funny, while big ladies and gentlemen remarked that we were so cute. Some were very indifferent to us and deliberately ignored us. So we had a time of uncertainty on a shelf in a showcase for so many months.\n\nOne day, we managed to impress a fine lady from Gl\u00fccksburg-Holnis, in Northern Germany. She was Dora. She took us both in her hand, set us on her palm carefully, and gazed at us sharply, studying how we looked. We heard her say to her husband Wilhelm that we both looked so cute. So they picked us from the shop, brought us home, and placed us on Dora\u2019s piano. We kept enjoying to the beautiful melodies she played on the piano, and had a jolly time, listening to the always theatrical conversations that took place with different personalities in their drawing room. Gamini was there in August 1990, and when he was leaving, along with many other toys, we were both given to him, as he and his wife Dammi had two small boys called Nivanka and Danilo. We were again safely packed in a brown paper bag and kept in Gamini\u2019s luggage until we were taken out on his return home."
