    "chunk_size_bytes": 1740,
    "chunk_text": "Hemas Holdings\u2019 stock trading near its estimated fair value\n\nFirst Capital Research (FCR) has downgraded its recommendation for Hemas Holdings PLC (HHL) from \u2018Hold\u2019 to \u2018Sell and Discontinue Coverage\u2019, advising investors to book profits as the stock is trading near its estimated fair value.\n\nThe decision follows HHL\u2019s broadly in-line quarterly results. The conglomerate\u2019s Consumer Brands segment posted a healthy 21.7% year-on-year revenue growth, with strong volumes. The Healthcare segment also showed momentum, with robust performance in pharmaceutical distribution and hospital services.\n\nDespite this solid operational performance, FCR maintains its fair value estimate for the stock at LKR 30.0 for FY26E and LKR 36.0 for FY27E. With HHL\u2019s current share price at LKR 34.6, the implied annualised return is seen as materially below the research firm\u2019s minimum required threshold.\n\nThe analyst report notes that the Healthcare segment, particularly manufacturing, has attractive long-term prospects while , the ongoing hospital expansion is not expected to significantly boost earnings for approximately three years.\n\nThe Consumer Brands segment is viewed as operating near peak capacity amidst competitive pressures.\n\nFCR concludes that the stock has achieved its fair value, leading to the downgrade. The move is presented as a valuation-based call, reflecting that the period of exceptional share price appreciation may have run its course for now, rather than a critique of the company\u2019s fundamental business strength.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
