    "chunk_size_bytes": 2015,
    "chunk_text": "Maxi was a consummate singer, a true professional, who had mastered vocal artistry, blending his power-packed voice with warm, sultry tones to convey the emotions as the song demanded, and all of this delivered with finesse.\n\nAmong my favourite duets with Maxi was \u2018Unforgettable\u2019 and our much-lauded version of \u2018Beauty and the Beast\u2019, which we performed \u2018live\u2019 at one of The Island Music Awards presentations.\n\nThe Late Maxi Rozairo: His memories are indelible and will be treasured for a lifetime\n\nI met up with Maxi, and his charming wife, my friend Yasmin, on his final visit to Melbourne, in January 2024. I took this opportunity to chat with him on a two-part interview on \u2018Music Matters\u2019, my regular TV programme in Australia, telecast on \u2018The Sri Lanka Morning Show\u2019 on Melbourne\u2019s Channel 31.\n\nHis response to my question on \u201cthe reason why we don\u2019t see him in action on stage these days\u201d, he regrettably gave a final ring to an illustrious career that spanned over 57years\u2026\u201cI hung my boots up 10 years ago\u201d.\n\nBesides being an accomplished singer, Maxi was also a family man, who would have his loving wife Yasmin join us for several overseas tours. I recall that she was, on one occasion, accompanied in Dubai, by their adorable little elder son Keith, who was five, at the time.\n\nThe entire group was a family unit, together with my late husband, Kenneth, the latter manager of the band, Kate Sabaratnam (wife of Mohan, who took over on Chinthi\u2019s departure) and others, including Raj Senewiratne\u2019s partner, Kate. (Raj took over from Raja Jalaldeen in Damascus).\n\nThose were exciting times filled with fun and laughter, horse riding by the Pyramids of Giza, the post- performance Scrabble games, the shopping sprees, the sing-songs, etc., etc\u2026Beautiful bonding!\n\nThese cherished memories were part of our reminiscences when I was blessed to meet up with my dear friend Maxi for the final time, together with Yasmin, on my recent visit to Colombo, in November, 2025."
  },
