    "chunk_text": "IQ Global and CLASS unveil region\u2019s first \u201cGeoStrategy Business Design\u201d programme\n\nAs geopolitical upheavals increasingly shape business outcomes, IQ Global has partnered with the Centre for Law & Security Studies (CLASS) to launch the region\u2019s first \u201cGeoStrategy \u00d7 Business Design\u201d programme, an initiative that aims to redefine how senior leaders prepare for a world where disruption has become the norm.\n\nFrom shifting trade alliances to sudden regulatory changes and supply chain disruptions triggered by distant conflicts, global volatility now reaches boardrooms with unprecedented speed. Many organisations find themselves drowning in information, yet lacking the framework to translate it into meaningful, timely action. The new programme is designed precisely to address this gap.\n\nCombining CLASS\u2019s geopolitical insight with IQ Global\u2019s expertise in business design and strategic transformation, the initiative introduces a simulation-driven, design-led approach to leadership. Participants will engage in scenario wargames, future-mapping exercises and decision-stress testing, tools that help leaders convert global signals into concrete strategic moves.\n\nNilanthan Niruthan, Director at CLASS, noted: \u201cThe distance between geopolitics and corporate strategy has collapsed. Leaders need clarity on which global shifts matter and what decisions must follow. This programme is built to provide exactly that.\u201d\n\nMelvin Mervyn, COO of IQ Global, added: \u201cEvery global headline now carries real operational consequences. Leaders don\u2019t just need information, they need a way to act on it quickly and confidently. This programme gives them a mechanism to cut through uncertainty and design organisations resilient enough to thrive in any future.\u201d"
