    "md5": "fa77185af132e911fc4b201045e61671",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1368,
    "chunk_text": "Magnanimity by Washington-based Lankans\n\nSri Lankans residing in Washington, United States, under the banner of the \u201cSri Lanka Ranga Kala Kavaya\u201d, have donated US dollars 6,500 to the \u201cRe-Building Sri Lanka\u201d fund this week.\n\nThe donation was made with the objective of supporting the restoration of livelihoods of people affected by the Dittwa cyclone and contributing to the rebuilding of areas damaged by the disaster, the organisation\u2019s Chairman, Anura Ratnayake, said. He noted that the initiative reflects the commitment of overseas Sri Lankans to stand with the motherland during times of crisis.\n\nThe cheque pertaining to the donation was formally handed over by Chairman Anura Ratnayake to Secretary to the President, Dr. Nandika Sanath Kumanayake, at a brief ceremony held this week.\n\nOfficials expressed appreciation for the gesture, stating that such contributions from the Sri Lankan diaspora play a vital role in strengthening national recovery and reconstruction efforts following natural disasters.\n\nFrom applause to adventure: Ceylinco Life achievers take wing again\n\nUber Eats 2025 Cravings Report: Sri Lankans crave spice, then reach for chocolate\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
