    "chunk_size_bytes": 1445,
    "chunk_text": "China has solidly reaffirmed its position as Sri Lanka\u2019s fifth-largest international tourism source market. In a strong signal of recovery and demand, Sri Lanka welcomed over 132,000 Chinese visitors in 2025.\n\nSriLankan Airlines in Guangzhou Passenger Sales Manager Li Shaojie underscored the vital air link between the two nations. \u201cSriLankan Airlines is proud to serve as the essential bridge connecting Guangzhou and Colombo,\u201d he stated. \u201cWe are committed to maintaining and optimising our flight schedule, which provides the only direct service from Guangzhou to Colombo. With four weekly flights and a flight time of just five and a half hours, we ensure seamless and convenient access for tourists and business partners alike.\u201d\n\nThe event was further highlighted by an immersive video presentation showcasing Sri Lanka\u2019s unique landscapes and rich tea culture. Participants had the opportunity to experience the country\u2019s breathtaking scenery through VR technology and to sample its world-renowned teas during a dedicated tasting session.\n\nThe evening concluded with a unified call for collaboration, firmly positioning Sri Lanka as a premier, resilient, and ready destination. The nation stands prepared to offer discerning Chinese travellers an exceptional blend of safety, stunning beauty, and unparalleled experiences from its sun-kissed beaches and ancient heritage to its vibrant wildlife and famously warm hospitality."
