    "chunk_text": "Phew! An impasse and a tricky situation were sorted. It was my \u201cFaux Pas\u201d and a good lesson learned in the need for checking translations to prevent cultural misunderstandings. Looking back on this incident, I realized where the original misunderstanding was. Even the original English meaning, according to the etymology of the word, was \u201can attendant in a noble household\u201d. In Arabic the word may have taken a pejorative meaning, that of \u201ca donkey\u2019s keeper\u201d. It was only later, even in English, that yeomen\u2019s service came to mean, \u201cgood, efficient service\u201d.\n\n(Excerpted from an anthology of memoirs by Nihal Kodituwakku) \u270d\ufe0f\n\nMy experience in turning around the Merchant Bank of Sri Lanka (MBSL)\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
