    "chunk_size_bytes": 1464,
    "chunk_text": "The proposal is to resettle them not where they were nor in near-by Wet Zone areas but in appropriate locations within the Dry Zone which are likely to be less congested. This will not only relieve Wet Zone rural congestion in the hilly terrains but also help Dry Zone development effort which has been an increasingly important strategy for us over a great many decades.\n\nThe proposed planned resettlement work identified here clearly requires the guidance of specialized professional expertise. Of particularly importance will be\n\nthose with appropriate prior experience in the RVDB\u2019s Walawe Ganga Project or in one of the three completed settlement efforts of the Mahaweli Project i.e. in Systems \u2018H\u2019, \u2018C\u2019 or most recently in System \u2018B\u2019.\n\nAlso, the expertise of Irrigation Engineers, Land Surveyors, Administrators and NBRI personnel, especially those with prior experience of Dry Zone resettlement projects will also be valuable for the execution of the proposed resettlement work. Many of these latter personnel could be found within the Irrigation, Agriculture, and Survey Departments or among their recent retirees, those from the former Mahaweli Development Board, the RVDB and also of course those currently available within the Mahaweli Authority.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
