    "md5": "4f165c510d9ae3129ed8ee7595a45ef2",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1980,
    "chunk_text": "Are we lying to our children?\n\nIf you have a child, grandchild, niece or nephew, what do you hope for their future? My guess is, you would hope they will become well-educated, responsible and active citizens, who have a respectable career, are married, and one day have a family of their own.\n\nSo, how do they get there? By being good children, we tell them. We often praise children for being \u2018good\u2019, usually from the time they are born. They are \u2018good\u2019 if they don\u2019t cry, if they are quiet, well-behaved, and don\u2019t make a fuss. They are \u2018good\u2019 if they are obedient, and do as they are told.\n\nI believe this is a lie. Being respectful, disciplined and honest is important. But always being good? Always doing what you\u2019re told? Never doing anything naughty? That sounds like a recipe for disaster.\n\nWhy do I say this? The child who is always \u2018good\u2019 probably doesn\u2019t make mistakes. They never fail. Never get a D. Never have a boyfriend or girlfriend. Doesn\u2019t go to parties. They enter adulthood with little idea of who they are, what they like, what they think, what matters to them or where they are heading. Most dangerous of all, they have little exposure to the realities of life. However, because they were \u2018good\u2019 children, no one, including themselves, is concerned. After all, they had good grades, were studious, stayed out of trouble and appeared on track to enter a good university.\n\nThey then reach their mid-twenties, and suddenly, everyone has forgotten about exam results. There is a new question on the tip of everyone\u2019s tongue, which is \u2018So, do you have a boyfriend/girlfriend?\u2019 This soon evolves to, \u2018So, when are you getting married?\u2019 and that child is confused. Boyfriends and girlfriends used to be \u2018bad\u2019, and now they are suddenly essential. They didn\u2019t realize there was another timeline, and a whole other set of goals they should have been thinking about. They don\u2019t know where to start. They are vulnerable."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
