    "md5": "d3529ec9d2c7591edb7a876cca769e08",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1620,
    "chunk_text": "They then reach their mid-twenties, and suddenly, everyone has forgotten about exam results. There is a new question on the tip of everyone\u2019s tongue, which is \u2018So, do you have a boyfriend/girlfriend?\u2019 This soon evolves to, \u2018So, when are you getting married?\u2019 and that child is confused. Boyfriends and girlfriends used to be \u2018bad\u2019, and now they are suddenly essential. They didn\u2019t realize there was another timeline, and a whole other set of goals they should have been thinking about. They don\u2019t know where to start. They are vulnerable.\n\nI propose freedom. Freedom to make mistakes. To be \u2018naughty\u2019 or \u2018bad\u2019 children, once in a while. Freedom to ask questions, have awkward, difficult conversations, argue, and think. Freedom to explore \u2013 places, people, experiences, different opinions and ways of living. Freedom to get hurt. Freedom to fail.\n\nFreedom is not possible without knowledge. Knowledge enables freedom, and also boundaries it. What topics matter? I suggest the following, in no particular order- how the human body works, how to live a truly \u2018healthy\u2019 life, how to be mindful, drugs (including cigarettes, electronic cigarettes and tobacco, and addiction), how to date respectfully, sexual and reproductive health, mental health, how to choose a life partner, how to argue, what it means to have integrity, how to use social media and AI, how to interpret information, and how to be financially secure. In addition, especially for girls, how to plan a career around having children and nurturing a family life, should also be included. I am sure there are many more topics."
  },
