    "md5": "995eac3e36ce8d47f47d4d3b5a9a572f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1853,
    "chunk_text": "Freedom is not possible without knowledge. Knowledge enables freedom, and also boundaries it. What topics matter? I suggest the following, in no particular order- how the human body works, how to live a truly \u2018healthy\u2019 life, how to be mindful, drugs (including cigarettes, electronic cigarettes and tobacco, and addiction), how to date respectfully, sexual and reproductive health, mental health, how to choose a life partner, how to argue, what it means to have integrity, how to use social media and AI, how to interpret information, and how to be financially secure. In addition, especially for girls, how to plan a career around having children and nurturing a family life, should also be included. I am sure there are many more topics.\n\nWhat happens if our children are not given freedom through knowledge? They will not be well-rounded children, and will not become well-rounded adults. They will be ill-prepared for the real world. What would this look like? A teenage girl who is so stressed about her A-levels that she gains weight, her periods stop, and she doesn\u2019t go out anymore. A marriage that has occurred between two people who do not know each other well, have unrealistic expectations of each other, or are wholly incompatible. A couple that cannot resolve their sexual problems and live their days out unhappily. Hiding mental or physical illness. In short, not knowing how to navigate the challenges of life, and not knowing how to access help.\n\nWhat a shame these situations are. They are all preventable, and still fixable. Instead, many people suffer the consequences of such situations their entire lives. If we think such issues will \u2018fall into place\u2019 and \u2018sort themselves out\u2019, we are being naive.\n\nLet us celebrate the \u2018bad\u2019 and \u2018naughty\u2019 children. Let us empower our children with knowledge and freedom."
  },
