    "chunk_size_bytes": 1551,
    "chunk_text": "NDB Bank supports national SME recovery initiative\n\nNDB Bank has reinforced its commitment to Sri Lanka\u2019s small and medium enterprises by participating in the \u2018Revive Sri Lanka | Rising Stronger\u2019 forum at Kandy City Centre. The event, attended by over 800 entrepreneurs and stakeholders, aimed to restore livelihoods and confidence following the recent DITWA cyclone.\n\nThe initiative highlighted crucial public-private collaboration for economic recovery, with the presence of Central Bank Governor Dr. Nandalal Weerasinghe and Central Province Chief Secretary G.H.M.A. Premasinghe. It united leading financial institutions in a show of sector-wide support.\n\nRepresenting NDB, Sanjaya Perera, Senior Vice President \u2013 Personal Banking and Customer Experience, emphasized the bank\u2019s dedication. \u201cThe resilience of our nation is built on the strength of its entrepreneurs. Supporting SMEs during disruption is a commitment we take seriously,\u201d he stated.\n\nNDB\u2019s involvement aligns with its mission to foster inclusive growth. Through tailored financial solutions and advisory support, the bank remains dedicated to helping Sri Lankan businesses navigate challenges and achieve sustainable recovery, underscoring the vital role of SMEs in employment and regional development.\n\nHayleys Chief Mohan Pandithage recognised as Businessman for Year 2025\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
