    "chunk_text": "5. Armenia addresses AI risks by focusing on four pillars: explainability (using clear, non-technical logic), transparency (open-source data), robust cybersecurity (aligned with ISO standards), and stakeholder engagement (involving tax firms, media, and civil society in oversight). In the future, an Algorithm Impact Assessment (AIA) could be carried out to mitigate the risks. AIA is a self-assessment carried out to determine the impact of the algorithm on the citizens to ensure privacy, ethics, and human rights.\n\nCentral to this framework is the concept of human-AI collaboration. Rather than viewing AI as a replacement for human workers, the framework emphasises the potential of combining human expertise with AI capabilities. This approach not only leads to superior outcomes but also helps to address concerns about job displacement and builds internal support for AI initiatives. By adopting a structured framework for AI implementation, IRD can harness the power of this transformative technology while maintaining public and investor trust, ensuring transparent tax administration for all citizens leading to a technology-led revolution which will secure the nation\u2019s economic future."
