    "md5": "f1eb82b5fa698e47d05e6facc72a8b92",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1929,
    "chunk_text": "COYLE announces return of Harvard\u2019s Boris Groysberg to host leadership masterclass\n\nAs the Sri Lankan business landscape undergoes a period of profound transition, the Chamber of Lankan Entrepreneurs (COYLE) announces the return of Harvard Business School (HBS) Professor Boris Groysberg for an exclusive three-day executive program this February. Targeted specifically at CEOs, Board Directors, and Senior Management, this masterclass arrives at a critical juncture for the national economy. This is far more than a traditional seminar; it is a high-intensity, transformative, and hands-on immersion into the strategies required to lead through volatility and emerge with a definitive competitive edge.\n\nProfessor Groysberg, a global authority on organisational behaviour and the \u201cportability of talent,\u201d will guide participants through a curriculum specifically designed for the complexities of the current market. The program centres on the vital pillars of \u2018Team Cohesion\u2019 and \u2018Strategic Foresight\u2019, enabling leaders to build unified executive teams capable of anticipating market shifts before they occur. It further addresses the urgent need for leadership resilience and people management, providing the tactical blueprints necessary to mitigate \u201cbrain drain\u201d and keep high-performers anchored during economic fluctuations. Moving beyond incremental change, the sessions will also challenge leaders to embrace Innovation and Radical Transformation to fundamentally reinvent their business models for a globalised economy.\n\nThe program distinguishes itself through the signature Harvard Case Study Method, a rigorous and interactive pedagogical approach that forces leaders to step into the shoes of global decision-makers. Participants will move beyond passive listening to analyse real-world crises and debate solutions, ensuring they leave with an actionable toolkit rather than just theoretical notes."
