    "md5": "449079495aed896f6edd1c4898bdf1b4",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1935,
    "chunk_text": "W.R. Rodrigo & Partners announces strategic transition to partnership\n\nW.R. Rodrigo and Co. has announced a formal transition in its professional structure, moving from a sole practitioner firm to a partnership. This evolution coincides with the appointment of Chanie Rodrigo as a Partner, joining Managing Partner Rajitha Rodrigo to lead the newly reconstituted firm, W.R. Rodrigo and Partners, Chartered Accountants. The transition marks a significant milestone in the firm\u2019s forty-year history, reflecting a strategic move to broaden technical leadership and reinforce governance frameworks in an increasingly complex regulatory environment.\n\nThe appointment of Chanie Rodrigo reinforces the firm\u2019s technical capabilities in taxation. With over fifteen years of experience in the Sri Lankan tax landscape, her professional background includes tenures at international audit firms, followed by senior group tax roles within the private sector. An Associate Member of the Institute of Chartered Accountants of Sri Lanka (ACA) and a Fellow of ACCA (UK), she also holds the Enrolled Agent (USA) designation and a Bachelor of Science degree in Applied Accounting from Oxford Brookes University. Her focus remains on the intersection of statutory compliance and practical tax advisory, ensuring the firm\u2019s technical approach remains aligned with evolving Sri Lankan tax laws and regulatory requirements.\n\nManaging Partner Rajitha Rodrigo brings a wealth of international and local expertise to the partnership. As an ACA, ACMA (UK), and CGMA member, Rajitha\u2019s career spans nearly a decade, including nearly a decade with an international audit firm in both Sri Lanka and Singapore. His experience in assurance and advisory services across various sectors provides the foundation for the firm\u2019s focus on professional stewardship and managing organisational responses to shifting political, economic, and technological landscapes."
