    "md5": "800a6993600b2050d88bef5ec07a23d9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1850,
    "chunk_text": "Marlbo expands portfolio with FLIR thermal imaging cameras\n\n\\Global technology continues to reshape the electrical and safety landscape. Sophisticated inspection instruments now enable early detection of loose electrical connections before they spark, identify heat loss from buildings, and locate individuals obscured by smoke during emergencies.\n\nThese capabilities are made possible through thermal imaging cameras, which have become essential in modern safety and inspection practices. Unlike conventional cameras, they detect infrared radiation emitted by objects and convert it into visual images, allowing users to identify temperature variations on or beneath surfaces, even in complete darkness or poor visibility.\n\nReflecting this importance, Marlbo Trading, to strengthen safety standards and expand access to advanced fault detection technologies, has added Teledyne FLIR thermal imaging cameras to its product portfolio.\n\nThis introduction brings globally recognised thermal imaging technology to local industries seeking reliable, high-performance inspection and safety solutions.\n\nOnce regarded as specialised tools, thermal imaging cameras are now widely used across industries. In buildings and homes, they help detect insulation defects, hidden moisture, and energy losses. In industrial environments, they enable maintenance teams to identify overheating equipment and electrical faults early, preventing breakdowns, fires, and costly shutdowns. Emergency services rely on thermal imaging to navigate smoke-filled spaces and locate people when every second counts.\n\nThe impact extends beyond efficiency to directly improving safety. By identifying abnormal heat patterns early, potential risks can be addressed before escalation. This proactive approach reduces downtime, lowers repair costs, and protects both people and property."
